# How to Override Every Built-in Profile

You rarely need to write a `GateProfile` from scratch. Create `.acdd/profile.yaml` (or `.acdd/profiles/<name>.yaml`) and set `inherit:` to any built-in profile or local file.

## Inheritance & patching rules

1. **Map merging**: `roles`, `commands`, `scope_args_by_pattern`, `proofs`, `guidance`, `contours`, and `gate_templates` merge by key. Setting `<key>: null` removes an inherited entry.
2. **Replacing vs. patching gates**:
   - `gates: [...]` replaces the inherited gate DAG completely.
   - `gates_patch: [...]` surgically modifies inherited gates by `id`, dotted cursor (`"tasks.build"`, `"blueprint_synthesis.review"`), or `- tasks:`.
   - `- <id_or_cursor>: null` deletes an inherited gate.
   - `after: <sibling_id>` or `before: <sibling_id>` inserts a new gate next to an existing sibling.
   - Setting a scalar property to `null` (e.g. `role: null`, `command: null`) clears the inherited value.
3. **Content pinning**: `inherit: .acdd/profile.yaml:9f3a1c2` pins the parent file by SHA-256 prefix (`7..=64` hex chars) and fails closed if the parent changes unexpectedly.

---

## 1. Overriding `base` (minimal custom pipeline)

Start from `base` when you want clean `worktree` isolation, core contours, and `limits`, while defining your own `gates:` from scratch:

```yaml
version: 2
inherit: base

commands:
  test_all: "npm test"

roles:
  worker:
    mode: subagent
    runner: "codex exec --full-auto -"

gates:
  - id: implement
    role: worker
    command: test_all
    proof: command
    pass: verify
  - id: verify
    command: test_all
    proof: command
    receipt: true
    save: { immutable: true, post: commit }
```

---

## 2. Overriding `code` (standard repository `.acdd/profile.yaml`)

`code` declares abstract `build_check` and `verify_all` slots. Override them in `.acdd/profile.yaml`, bind `scope_args_by_pattern`, route models or external `runner:` CLIs, and insert custom gates with `gates_patch`:

```yaml
version: 2
inherit: code
tags: [default, docs]

commands:
  build_check:
    command: "pytest -q {scope_target} {test_filter}"
    test_filter: "-k {test}"
  verify_all:
    command: "ruff check . && pytest -q"
    timeout_seconds: 1200
  sec_scan: "cargo audit -q"

scope_args_by_pattern:
  "src/billing/**": "tests/billing/"
  "tests/*.py": "{file_stem}.py"

roles:
  builder:
    models: [claude-sonnet-4, gemini-4-hydrogen-high]
    reuse_on_reject: true
  independent_reviewer:
    models: [claude-opus-4]

gates_patch:
  - id: tasks.build
    max_attempts: 4
    checks:
      - code.seam
      - check: code.lint
        with: { categories: [arch, syntax, docs] }
  - id: security_gate
    after: run_tests
    command: sec_scan
    proof: command
    pass: integration_review
    fail: polish
```

---

## 3. Overriding `audit` (custom security contours & CLI runner)

`audit` runs read-only (`git.isolation: in_place`, `save: none`). Override it to add custom `contours`, enforce `code.lint` AST rules during `analyze`, customize report output paths, or attach a headless `auditor.runner`:

```yaml
version: 2
inherit: audit

roles:
  auditor:
    runner: "claude -p --permission-mode plan"

contours:
  sql_safety:
    description: "Verify all SQL queries use parameterized bindings or read-only connections."
    criteria:
      - "Inspect every SQLite/Postgres call site via code_map_impact."

gates_patch:
  - id: analyze
    contours: [correctness, security, architecture, sql_safety]
    checks:
      - check: code.lint
        with: { categories: [arch] }
  - id: triage
    save:
      immutable: true
      post: none
      report: ".acdd/reports/security-{run_name}.md"
```

---

## 4. Overriding `documentation` (custom doc scope & rules)

`documentation` verifies docs and `acdd-rule` invariants without needing a compiler. Override `polish` scope, disable an unnecessary gate, or add link/style checks:

```yaml
version: 2
inherit: documentation

commands:
  spell_check: "typos docs/ README.md"

gates_patch:
  - id: verify_docs
    command: spell_check
    checks:
      - docs.links
      - check: code.lint
        with: { categories: [arch, docs] }
  - id: polish
    scope: ["docs/**", "README.md", "CHANGELOG.md"]
```

---

## 5. Overriding `spec_planning` (custom spec output & reviewer)

`spec_planning` validates `acdd.yaml` `specs.*` collections and wave disjointness. Override `roles` to bind your preferred planning model or adjust `save.report`:

```yaml
version: 2
inherit: spec_planning

roles:
  architect:
    models: [gemini-4-neon-xhigh]
  independent_reviewer:
    models: [claude-opus-4]

gates_patch:
  - id: synthesize
    max_attempts: 4
  - id: review
    save:
      immutable: true
      report: ".acdd/reports/plan-review-{spec_id}.md"
```

---

## 6. Layering a `hotfix` overlay on `.acdd/profile.yaml`

Place sibling overlays under `.acdd/profiles/` (e.g. `.acdd/profiles/hotfix.yaml`). By inheriting `.acdd/profile.yaml`, you keep all repository `commands` and `scope_args_by_pattern` while pruning milestone-only gates:

```yaml
version: 2
inherit: .acdd/profile.yaml

gates_patch:
  - blueprint_synthesis: null
  - id: run_tests
    pass: handoff
  - integration_review: null
  - id: handoff
    need: [run_tests]
    guidance: [milestone.handoff, core.execution, hitl.pro]
```

Run it anytime via:

```sh
acdd start --goal "Fix billing timeout" --profile hotfix --scope src/billing/
```
